From 3d085806b7e00f9fe876b4fc1edd9cb862bc6664 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Himess <semihcvlk53@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:27:32 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] feat(host-contracts): ACL v0.10.0 with the E2 retirement
 certificate (lifecycle Level 3)

retireAccountWithSig(account, successor, chainIds, signature): anyone may
relay an account's signed retirement to the chains it lists. Checks, in
order: not retired; block.chainid listed; successor is the confirmed one
(non-null); the signature, code-first (no code: 65-byte low-s ECDSA; any
code, a 7702 indicator included: ERC-1271, no fallback). EIP-712 domain
("DecryptionAuthorityLifecycle", "1"), chain-agnostic. The effects are
those of retireAccount(); the certificate grants and changes nothing, has
no nonce or expiry, and is not pause-gated. ERC-165 0x4b9ec076.

Version 0.10.0, reinitializer 11, reinitializeV10() (no new state). The
upgrade matrix moves the v0.8.0 -> v0.9.0 cases onto a v0.9.0 fixture and
adds v0.9.0 -> v0.10.0 (U9): E1 state is preserved and a certificate works
right after the upgrade.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
